pi auth_failed invalid issuer.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"excluded_red_herrings\": [\n    {\n      \"signal\": \"orders-db CPU at 86%\",\n      \"why_not_primary\": \"The database reported normal 35 ms query p95 and zero errors, and no failed checkout transaction reached it because requests were stopped at the payment auth gate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"signal\": \"cdn-edge HTTP 5xx rate of 4.8%\",\n      \"why_not_primary\": \"The metric notes the failures were isolated to images; checkout logs say static assets recovered while the checkout flow remained blocked. This does not explain the issuer-specific 401 chain.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"signal\": \"JWKS cache miss with partner-v1 fallback\",\n      \"why_not_primary\": \"This is a contributing manifestation of the auth-gateway configuration inconsistency introduced by AUTH-2026-0318, not an independent upstream service failure.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recommended_next_steps\": [\n    \"Immediately restore auth-gateway allowed_issuers to partner-v2, or revert AUTH-2026-0318 using the approved rollback path.\",\n    \"Refresh or invalidate the affected JWKS cache namespace, then verify partner-v2 token validation succeeds.\",\n    \"Run a synthetic checkout through payment authorization and confirm HTTP 401 rates and checkout p95 return to baseline across auth-gateway, payment-api, and checkout-web.\",\n    \"After recovery, audit issuer and JWKS namespace rollout configuration and add a deployment gate that rejects mismatched issuer allowlists.\"\n  ]\n}\n"},"intent":"Write root cause assessment"}
